Z||000001||G-Nasty||12-27-2001||09:52 PM||||This has happened to me twice. Do not pump the peddle before you bleed it. I actually had a wrecker come and tow my car off and had a repairshop fix it back in the days...I think they used a machine to pressure bleed.<BR>You shouldnt have to do that however just: Press clutch pedal in fully and hold.<BR>Open the bleed screw and allow fluid to escape. <BR>Close bleed screw. <BR>Release pedal completely <BR>Top off fluid in reservoir. ||||reg||1
